    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d208">

                <pb facs="0641" n="583" sameAs="frus:frus1866p3/pg583"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Burton</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 159.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1866-11-09"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 9, 1866.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    despatch No. 275, of last September, containing a copy of a note addressed to
                    you by the minister of foreign affairs upon the subject of a contemplated
                    insurrection on the isthmus against the national government of Colombia. This
                    subject has come before this department on a former occasion, and you will find
                    instructions for your guidance set forth in the despatch to you on the 9th of
                    last month, No. 156.</p>
                <p>Your assurance to the minister of foreign affairs anticipated the spirit of that
                    despatch, and is therefore approved.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM. H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Allan A. Burton</hi>, Esq., &amp;<hi
                            rendition="#italic">c</hi>., &amp; <hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>.,
                            &amp;<hi rendition="#italic"> c</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
